    "body": "## Overview\n\nFixes the intermittent failure in `:amd: (MI355) Fusion and Compile FP8`: [Buildkite #94104](https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/94104/list?jid=01a12e24-6a90-4b79-b882-a91da3ba7420&tab=output).\n\n```\nFAILED tests/compile/correctness_e2e/test_attn_quant.py::test_rocm_aiter_static_attention_output_correctness\nAssertionError: Results for model='...Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct-FP8' are not the same.\n\nref_result=    {'test': 'seeded_sampling', 'text': ' Yvonne Cohen and', ...}\ncompare_result={'test': 'seeded_sampling', 'text': ' Tony and I'm an',  ...}\n```\n\nThe test was added in [#58099](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/58099) and pinned to the v1 model runner from the start. [#61014](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/61014) removed that pin as part of the MRV1 cleanup, so it now runs on v2 for the first time.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Only the `seeded_sampling` comparison fails. Every `temperature=0.0` comparison matches, and the unit tests for the same fusion pass with `atol=rtol=1e-2`.\n- Fusing output quantization drops a bf16 round-trip, so the two settings agree on the argmax but not on the exact distribution. Sampling at `temperature=1.0` over a 128k vocabulary turns that into a different token.\n- The forward pass is bit-identical on v1 and v2, and the fused/unfused gap is the same size on both. What changed is that the v2 sampler draws a different token for seed 33, and that one sits close enough to a boundary to flip. The pin was hiding the problem rather than preventing it.\n- This PR compares greedy output only, as [#41102](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/41102) already does for the cpu offload test. The five greedy comparisons and the assertion that the fusion fires in all 32 layers are unchanged.\n\n## Measurements\n\nMeasured on MI355 by running both settings as servers and asking each the same 100 seeded prompts, plus the top-20 logprobs of the first token:\n\n| compared | seeds that disagree | max abs delta logprob |\n|---|---|---|\n| unfused vs unfused | 0 / 100 | 0.000000 |\n| fused vs fused | 17 / 100 | 0.045204 |\n| unfused vs fused | 21 / 100 | 0.158091 |\n\nThe unfused path is reproducible across server starts; the fused one is not, so no choice of seed or tolerance makes an exact-equality check on sampled tokens stable here. Greedy output was identical in all of the above.\n\n## Validation\n\n`pytest -v -s tests/compile/correctness_e2e/test_attn_quant.py` on MI355:\n\n- before, on v2: fails with the strings above\n- with `VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER=0`: passes\n- after this change, on v2: passes in 115.69 s, with `rewrite counts: [32]`\n\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [ ] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [ ] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [ ] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
